description:
Ryan approved 2026-10-26. Today the Papyrus HN router POSTs one machine `decide` per publication and polls each job. The engine already makes ONE shared decision per item for all classifiers (decide_with_shared_context) and reuses it, but each call costs a full worker job (about 45 s). With six publications, router runs hit time_budget after about 3 stories. Goal: one request and one worker job per story, answering every requested publication.

## Contract (machine, SigV4, same principals as /machine/publications/*)

POST /machine/decisions
- Headers: X-Cyclotron-Account (selects a configured standing target, same as today).
- Body: {"contractVersion": "cyclotron-publication/v1", "requestId": "<8-128 [A-Za-z0-9._:-]>", "payload": {"bindings": {"<publicationId>": "<bindingRevision>", ...}, "item": {"id": ..., "values": {...}}}}
- Rules:
  - every key in bindings must be a binding of that standing target, with an equal revision (else 409 "publication binding changed");
  - at least 1 key; no pendingOutputs among them (else 409 "publication criteria are pending");
  - the item is validated exactly as in the single decide (validate_item);
  - allow_live is required (else 503);
  - request-id idempotency, run_busy, 403 and 503 semantics are the same as the single decide.
- Response 202: {contractVersion, accountId, runId, jobId, status, bindings: {...echo}}.

GET /machine/decisions/{jobId} (same headers)
- 202 while pending or running.
- 200 when done: {contractVersion, accountId, runId, jobId, decisionId, publications: {"<publicationId>": <exactly the object today's GET /machine/publications/{pub}/commands/{job} returns for that publication>}}.
- Refusals use the same codes and shapes as the single receipt (e.g. 429 request_ceiling, 503 provider_key_unavailable).

## Implementation notes
- Worker: one job kind (e.g. "publication-decisions") runs the native decide once and projects the response per publication with the existing per-publication projection (publication_lab.py:117-128). It must NOT run the extra per-publication status command per publication; at most one status, or none if not needed for the receipt.
- Keep the existing per-publication routes unchanged (backward compatible).
- Machine feedback is unchanged (still per publication).

## Acceptance (specs beside the modules, fake provider, no network)
- one POST for N=3 publications makes one job and one model request, and the receipt has three projections whose decisionId is equal;
- a mismatched revision for any publication gives 409 and creates no job;
- a pending output gives 409;
- the same requestId returns the same job, and a different body with the same requestId gives 409 request_conflict;
- 202 while running, then 200;
- the per-publication projections are byte-identical to what the existing single-publication receipt returns for the same decision;
- an offline benchmark shows worker jobs per story drop from N to 1.

## Router side (Papyrus, built by Papyrus implementation)
One POST per story with all configured publications' bindings, one poll, fan out per-publication `checked` into the ROUTE receipt as today. Fall back to per-publication decide when the lab answers 404 for /machine/decisions, so either side can deploy first.
